            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>Major Iron Ore Belts of Chhattisgarh: Bailadila & Dalli-Rajhara</h3>\n            <p>Chhattisgarh is India’s second-largest iron ore producing state (contributing ~16%–18% of national output). The state is renowned for super-high-grade hematite deposits of extraordinary purity, concentrated in the <strong>Dantewada</strong> (Bailadila) and <strong>Durg/Balod</strong> (Dalli-Rajhara) districts.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. The Bailadila Range (Dantewada District)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Geographical Setting:</strong> Located in the Bastar plateau (Dantewada district). The mountain range resembles the <em>hump of an ox</em>, hence the local name <strong>'Bailadila'</strong> (Bail = bull/ox; Dila = hump).</li>\n                <li><strong>Mineral Super-Grade:</strong> Hosts <strong>14 distinct high-grade hematite deposits</strong> along a 40 km ridge. The ore is exceptionally rich, assaying <strong>66% to 68% metallic iron (Fe)</strong> with minimal phosphorus and sulfur impurities, ranking among the best naturally occurring ores in the world.</li>\n                <li><strong>Mechanized Operations by NMDC:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>Operated by the <strong>National Mineral Development Corporation (NMDC)</strong> since 1968.</li>\n                        <li>Key production complexes: <em>Deposit 14, Deposit 11C, Deposit 5, and Deposit 10</em>. Deposit 5 is one of the largest single mechanized open-cast iron ore faces in Asia.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n                <li><strong>The Kirandul-Kottavalasa (KK) Railway Line:</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li>An engineering marvel passing through the Eastern Ghats (Ananthagiri hills, Araku Valley), featuring 58 tunnels and 84 major bridges.</li>\n                        <li>Built specifically to transport Bailadila iron ore over 450 km to <strong>Visakhapatnam Port</strong> for maritime export to <strong>Japan and South Korea</strong> under long-term bilateral agreements, as well as supplying the <strong>Rashtriya Ispat Nigam Limited (RINL / Vizag Steel Plant)</strong>.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. Dalli-Rajhara Range (Durg / Balod District)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>A 32 km long hematite ridge located in the Balod/Durg district of central Chhattisgarh.</li>\n                <li><strong>Captive Lifeline of Bhilai:</strong> Developed in the late 1950s by SAIL to serve as the captive iron ore mine for India’s premier Soviet-assisted public steel plant—the <strong>Bhilai Steel Plant (BSP)</strong>.</li>\n                <li><strong>The Rowghat Project:</strong> As Dalli-Rajhara deposits face exhaustion, SAIL is developing the massive <strong>Rowghat iron ore deposits</strong> in the Narayanpur/Kanker districts of northern Bastar to ensure a 30-year feedstock supply for Bhilai Steel.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. Other Producing Areas in Chhattisgarh</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Iron ore occurrences and quarries in <strong>Bilaspur, Rajnandgaon, and Kabirdham</strong> districts (Direct PDF Data).</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
