            "id": "m12",
            "title": "Major Manganese Belts: Balaghat, Nagpur-Bhandara, Keonjhar & MOIL Operations",
            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <h3>Major Manganese Belts: Geological Clusters & MOIL Operations</h3>\n            <p>Manganese deposits in India occur predominantly in metamorphic rocks of the Archean Dharwar System, forming stratiform tabular bodies associated with gondite and kodurite rock suites.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. The Madhya Pradesh-Maharashtra Central Belt (The Sausar Group)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>The most valuable and high-grade manganese province in India, stretching as an east-west arc across the <strong>Sausar Group</strong> of rocks through Balaghat and Chhindwara (MP) into Nagpur and Bhandara (Maharashtra).</li>\n                <li><strong>Balaghat & Chhindwara (Madhya Pradesh):</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><strong>Bharveli Mine:</strong> Located near Balaghat town; Asia's premier mechanized underground manganese mine, reaching depths over 350 meters with high-capacity vertical hoisting shafts. Produces super-grade metallurgical ore ($Mn \\ge 48\\%$).</li>\n                        <li><strong>Ukwa Mine:</strong> Features a historic 28-km long aerial ropeway for ore transport.</li>\n                        <li><strong>Tirodi & Sitapatore:</strong> Major open-pit and semi-underground operations.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n                <li><strong>Nagpur & Bhandara (Maharashtra):</strong>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><strong>Dongri Buzurg (Bhandara):</strong> A unique deposit of high-grade pyrolusite peroxide ore ($MnO_2$), essential for battery and chemical industries.</li>\n                        <li><strong>Mansar & Kandri (Nagpur):</strong> Large-scale underground mines operated by MOIL.</li>\n                        <li><strong>Gumgaon & Chikla:</strong> Productive mines along the Sausar metasedimentary belt.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>2. The Odisha Belt (Keonjhar, Sundargarh & Koraput)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Hosted within the Iron Ore Group (IOG) and Gangpur Group in northern Odisha.</li>\n                <li><strong>Barbil-Jamda-Koira Belt (Keonjhar):</strong> Manganese occurs intimately associated with iron ore in the horse-shoe synclinorium. High-phosphorus content in some deposits requires blending with Central Indian low-phosphorus ores.</li>\n                <li><strong>Sundargarh:</strong> Bisra, Birmitrapur, and Kumarmunda.</li>\n                <li><strong>Koraput & Rayagada:</strong> Nishikhal and Podakana deposits.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <h4>3. MOIL Limited (The National Manganese Champion)</h4>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Originally incorporated in 1896 as the <em>Central Provinces Manganese Ore Company (CPMO)</em>, taken over by the Government of India in 1962 as <strong>Manganese Ore (India) Limited (MOIL)</strong>.</li>\n                <li>A Miniratna Category-I CPSE under the Ministry of Steel, headquartered in <strong>Nagpur</strong>.</li>\n                <li>Produces over <strong>50% of India’s domestic manganese ore</strong> and operates 11 mines across MP and Maharashtra.</li>\n            </ul>\n        ",
            "pointsToRemember": [
                "The Sausar Group across MP and Maharashtra is India's premier high-grade manganese geological belt.",
                "Balaghat houses the iconic Bharveli mine (Asia's largest underground manganese mine, 48%+ Mn).",
                "Dongri Buzurg in Bhandara yields high-purity peroxide ore used in batteries.",
                "Nagpur mines include Mansar, Kandri, and Gumgaon.",
                "Odisha's manganese is concentrated in the Barbil-Jamda-Koira valley of Keonjhar.",
                "MOIL Limited (headquartered in Nagpur) produces over 50% of India's domestic manganese output."
            ],
            "keyNotes": [
                "The Sausar metasedimentary belt spanning Balaghat (MP) and Nagpur-Bhandara (Maharashtra) houses MOIL's premier underground mines, anchoring India's manganese self-sufficiency."
            ],
